[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-30 10:52:57\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.1s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.1s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/cortex/memory/vector_store.py:191: UserWarning: Api key is used with an insecure connection.\r\n  self._client = AsyncQdrantClient(url=self._url, api_key=self._api_key)\r\n  [  1.1s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/qdrant_client/async_qdrant_remote.py:225: UserWarning: Qdrant client version 1.18.0 is incompatible with server version 1.16.3. Major versions should match and minor version difference must not exceed 1. Set check_compatibility=False to skip version check.\r\n  show_warning(\r\n  [  8.5s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [  8.5s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [  8.5s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 10.3s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 10.3s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 10.3s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 10.3s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 16.1s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 16.1s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 16.1s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 91.2s]          drafting the report from 6 observation(s)\r\n  [148.6s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [148.6s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (6.1s); missing: Stage-by-stage breakdown of closed-lost deals showing which pipeline stage they were in immediately before being marked closed-lost (current data only shows final closedlost stage, not the stage they fell out of); Historical stage-transition/audit-log data per deal to identify where in the funnel deals stall or drop; Full unpaginated closed-lost dataset (only 100 of 225 records returned) to compute accurate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s and value totals per prior stage; Comparable data on deals that progressed successfully through each stage, to compute stage-specific loss rates rather than raw \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s\r\n  sufficiency gate withheld 1 causal claim(s)\r\n  [169.4s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 149s over 3 steps, 70,083 tokens, 6 observations gathered, 3 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  By \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, losses (\u2588\u2588\u2588) vastly outnumber wins (\u2588\u2588) over Jan\u2013Sep \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, and by value, the known lost amount among a \u2588\u2588\u2588-deal sample ($\u2588.\u2588\u2588M) already exceeds the total won amount ($\u2588.\u2588\u2588M) \u2014 with true lost value likely higher since \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals and n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 half the amount fields remain unexamined or unpopulated.  [hubspot.search 702aed37, hubspot.search 99c87eae]\r\n  As a proxy, the current open pipeline shows the heaviest concentration of deals (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588) sitting at 'presentationscheduled', suggesting this is the most likely stall point worth investigating \u2014 but this is inferred from where deals currently sit, not a direct measurement of where they were lost.  [hubspot.pipeline 4d626ba8]\r\n  The immediate fix is process, not \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: start recording the stage-at-loss on every closed-lost deal so this question can be answered with data rather than inference going forward.  [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Closed-lost records do not preserve the stage the deal died at  (high)\r\n    - Every one of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deal records inspected in detail carries stage = 'closedlost', with no field indicating which pipeline stage (e.g. presentationscheduled, qualifiedtobuy) the deal was in before it was marked lost.  [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n    - This means the question 'which stage are we losing deals at' cannot be answered directly from the closed-lost data as currently modeled in HubSpot \u2014 it is a data-collection gap, not an absence of losses.  [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n  Losses vastly outnumber wins over the period, and known lost value already exceeds total won value  (medium)\r\n    - Between 2026-01-01 and 2026-09-30, \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals closed lost versus only \u2588\u2588 deals closed won \u2014 a roughly \u2588\u2588:\u2588 ratio of lost to won deal \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588.  [hubspot.search 702aed37, hubspot.search 99c87eae]\r\n    - Among the \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals examined in detail, \u2588\u2588 carry a recorded amount summing to $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, which already exceeds the $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total amount across all \u2588\u2588 closed-won deals in the same window \u2014 and this is before ac\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ing for the other \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals not yet read.  [hubspot.search 702aed37, hubspot.search 99c87eae]\r\n    - \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals sampled have no amount recorded at all, meaning the true lost-value figure is under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d and cannot be precisely quantified from this data.  [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] Most deals are lost at the presentation/demo stage (presentationscheduled), consistent with it being the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st bucket of stalled open pipeline.\r\n      The open-pipeline stage distribution is a proxy for where deals accumulate, not a direct record of where lost deals died, since closed-lost records do not retain a pre-close stage. The concentration at presentationscheduled is suggestive but not verified against actual loss events.\r\n  [contradicted] Deals are lost overwhelmingly at the earliest stages (stage_\u2588 / appointmentscheduled), i.e. weak top-of-funnel qualification.\r\n      If \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-stage attrition were the dominant loss pattern, the open pipeline would show few deals surviving past stage_\u2588/appointmentscheduled. Instead only \u2588 of \u2588\u2588 open deals sit at those two earliest stages combined, while \u2588\u2588 have advanced past them, making \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-stage die-off an unlikely primary explanation.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Add or start populating a 'stage at time of loss' property on deals going forward (e.g. snapshot the stage before transitioning to closedlost), so future analysis can directly answer which funnel stage sheds the most deals and value.\r\n      why: Without this, the question 'which stage are we losing deals at' cannot be answered directly from HubSpot data \u2014 every closed-lost deal currently shows the terminal stage only.\r\n      [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n  P\u2588 Given the current pipeline's heavy concentration of open deals at presentationscheduled, prioritize reviewing win/loss notes and rep feedback for deals sitting in that stage to identify friction points (e.g. demo quality, competitive positioning, pricing objections raised post-demo).\r\n      why: \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 open deals ($ majority of pipeline) sit at presentationscheduled, the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st single stage bucket, making it the most plausible \u2014 though unconfirmed \u2014 point of stall and eventual loss.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 4d626ba8]\r\n  P\u2588 Backfill amount values on historical closed-lost deals where possible, and read the remaining \u2588\u2588\u2588 unread lost-deal records, before reporting a firm total lost-value figure.\r\n      why: \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled lost deals have no amount, and \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 total lost deals were not yet examined, so the current $\u2588.\u2588\u2588M figure under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s true lost value and should not be treated as final.\r\n      [hubspot.search 702aed37]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The closed-lost stage field is uniformly 'closedlost' with no historical stage trail, so any conclusion about 'which stage' deals are lost at is inference from the current open-pipeline snapshot, not a measurement of actual loss events. This could be materially wrong if deals that die at earlier stages are simply deleted or never logged as 'closedlost' with full history.\r\n  - \u2588\u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals were not read in full detail (only a \u2588\u2588\u2588-row sample was examined), so the $\u2588.\u2588\u2588M lost-value figure and the \u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588 amount-populated split are drawn from less than half the total lost deals and likely under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 true lost value.\r\n  - N\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 half of sampled closed-lost deals (\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588) have no amount value recorded, meaning true dollar impact of losses cannot be reliably totaled.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: asked as an open question, with this claim withheld, the same evidence does not establish a cause: This shows a list of closed-lost deals between Jan-Sep \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (\u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching, \r\n- executive_summary[2]: The evidence confirms \u2588\u2588 total deals and shows several at 'presentationscheduled', but the truncated payload doesn't allow verification of the specific \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 deals in that st\r\n- findings[1].claims[1]: The evidence confirms the $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 sum for the \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals, the $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total for the \u2588\u2588 won deals, and \u2588\u2588\u2588 remaining unread lost deals, but the truncated payload never sta\r\n- findings[1].claims[2]: The evidence shows many records with null amount among the \u2588\u2588\u2588 returned, but the truncated payload does not confirm the exact \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 null-amount records.\r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. The observations show total \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s of closed-lost and closed-won deals but do not record which funnel stage each lost deal was in before being marked lost, so no stage-level loss ranking (by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 or value) can be derived, let alone a recommended fix. The data describes outcomes but not the funnel location or mechanism of loss. What would settle it: Stage-by-stage breakdown of closed-lost deals showing which pipeline stage they were in immediately before being marked closed-lost (current data only shows final closedlost stage, not the stage they fell out of); Historical stage-transition/audit-log data per deal to identify where in the funnel deals stall or drop; Full unpaginated closed-lost dataset (only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 records returned) to compute accurate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s and value totals per prior stage; Comparable data on deal\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-lost deal records show stage='closedlost' uniformly with no retained pre-close stage, preventing direct stage-of-loss analysis.\r\n  - Only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 matching closed-lost deals were read in detail; conclusions about lost value are based on this partial sample.\r\n  - \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled closed-lost deals have no amount field populated, understating true lost dollar value.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  4d626ba8  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  702aed37  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-01-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n  99c87eae  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-01-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (169s wall, 167s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1    0.993    1%   0.993  no model call\r\n  recall           1    0.029    0%   0.029  no model call\r\n  loop_model       3     88.4   52%    29.5  in 6 out 8,677 cached 20,594\r\n  loop_tools       2      1.8    1%   0.880  no model call\r\n  draft            1     57.4   34%    57.4  in 55,946 out 5,454\r\n  gate             1    0.031    0%   0.031  no model call\r\n  verify           1     12.5    7%    12.5  in 53,126 out 1,677\r\n  sufficiency      1      6.1    4%     6.1  in 4,090 out 316\r\n  unmeasured              2.3    1%\r\n  cache hit rate: 15%\r\n"]
